WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.000
Payload is a configured-system claim.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.440
The Meta O R W design specification states a minimum equipment payload

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.440
of four thousand seven hundred kilograms with allowed support bracing or stiffening.

4
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.680
The equipment payload excludes the rack frame's own mass.

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.540
The document also explains that equipment design and arrangement affect frame capability.

6
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.120
Read the permitted support and configuration conditions rather than copying the number

7
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.960
into a universal O R W rating.

8
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:30.500
Static support, transport, lifting and relocation are different cases and may require

9
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:31.220
different evidence.

10
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.400
For the proposed assembly, identify the equipment distribution, center of gravity, braces,

11
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.220
accessories and handling state.

12
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.560
Ask which qualification record supports that configuration and which changes require reassessment.

13
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.680
A larger nominal payload doesn't prove that the floor, lift, wheels, attachments

14
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.000
or transport route support the loaded assembly.

15
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:55.660
The acceptance decision needs the relevant configured evidence, not a number detached

16
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.120
from the structure and test conditions that make it meaningful.

